.TH GSURFCTL 1 "2026" "gsurf 0.4.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gsurfctl \- drive a running gsurf from the shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gsurfctl
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGUMENTS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gsurfctl
talks to the control socket every
.BR gsurf (1)
opens (JSON-RPC 2.0 over a Unix socket in
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/gsurf/<pid>-XXXXXX/control.sock ,
owner-only; see
.I docs/control.org
under
.IR @DATADIR@/doc/gsurf ).
It opens and lists tabs, reads pages, runs JavaScript and key-binding
actions, switches the input mode, drives wmux panes and windows, reads the
configuration, toggles modules and follows events.
.PP
The instance is the one given with
.B \-S
or
.BR \-i ,
else
.BR $GSURF_INSTANCE ,
else the only one running, else the most recently focused one.
.PP
Options may come before or after the command;
.B \-\-
ends them. The words after
.BR wmux ,
.B eval
and
.B call
are taken literally.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-instance =\fIID\fR
The instance: a pid, a
.B control.name
or a runtime directory id.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-socket =\fIPATH\fR
A control socket instead of an instance.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Send the command to every running instance.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Print results as JSON.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pretty
Indent JSON.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-timeout =\fIS\fR
Seconds to wait for a reply (default 30; 0 forever).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print nothing on success.
.TP
.BR \-\-completion =\fIbash\fR
Print the bash completion script.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.B \-\-license
Print the license.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
The running instances.
.TP
.B info
pid, version, backend, name, windows, views, focus time.
.TP
.BR open " [\fIURL\fR] [\fB\-\-bg\fR] [\fB\-\-container\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-child\-of\fR \fIVIEW\fR]"
Open a tab (an existing file path opens as file://).
.TP
.BR nav " \fIURL\fR, " back ", " forward ", " stop ", " reload " [\fB\-\-hard\fR]"
Load, history, reload.
.TP
.BR tabs ", " tab " \fIVIEW\fR, " close " [\fIVIEW\fR]"
List, switch to, close views (ids).
.TP
.BR tree ", " move " \fIVIEW\fR \fB\-\-parent\fR|\fB\-\-before\fR|\fB\-\-after\fR|\fB\-\-index\fR \fIN\fR, " collapse " \fIVIEW\fR [on|off]"
The tab tree.
.TP
.BR containers ", " reopen " \fIVIEW CONTAINER\fR"
Containers; reopen a view in another one.
.TP
.BR title ", " uri ", " text ", " eval " \fIJS\fR, " screenshot " \fIFILE\fR"
The page.
.TP
.BR actions ", " action " \fINAME\fR, " mode " [normal|insert]"
Key-binding actions and the input mode.
.TP
.BR panes ", " windows ", " wmux " \fI'COMMAND'\fR, " select\-window " \fIN\fR, " rename\-window " \fIN\fR [\fINAME\fR]"
wmux panes and windows.
.TP
.BR config " [\fIKEY\fR], " modules ", " module " \fINAME\fR [on|off], " methods
Configuration, modules, the socket's methods.
.TP
.BR watch " [\fITOPIC\fR...]"
Print events (view, uri, title, load, mode, layout, download) until
interrupted.
.TP
.BR call " \fIMETHOD\fR [\fIJSON\fR|\fIKEY=VALUE\fR...]"
A raw JSON-RPC call.
.TP
.BR help " [\fICOMMAND\fR|\fB\-\-names\fR]"
Help, one command's usage, or the command names.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 ok; 1 the command failed; 2 usage error; 3 no instance (or it could not be
reached); 4 refused by kiosk mode.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GSURF_INSTANCE
The default instance.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Where instances are found.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
gsurfctl open https://example.org \-\-bg
gsurfctl \-j tabs
gsurfctl wmux 'split\-window \-h https://github.com'
gsurfctl mode insert
gsurfctl watch view uri
gsurfctl \-i work open https://mail.example.org
gsurfctl call open uri=https://example.org background=true
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gsurf (1)
